Create a simple modal dialog for situations where you want to prompt the user before continuing.
The component is first rendered as a button on the page as shown in the PatternFly-React example. When the user clicks the button then the modal is shown. A future version of this component could allow the developer to use other initial components instead of a button. For example, you might want to use a link instead.
By default, the modal will have localized "Continue" and "Cancel" buttons. The labels on these buttons can be overridden in parameters passed to the component.
All string parameters accept a localization key which is localized as the component is rendered.
Sample usage:
{code:javascript}
import * as React from 'react';
import {ContinueCancelModal} from '../../widgets/ContinueCancelModal';
export class MyClass extends React.Component<MyProps> {
 private doSometing = () => {
 // do something on Continue
 // See for 
 // more ways to pass functions
 }
 public render(): React.ReactNode {
 <React.Fragment>
 <ContinueCancelModal 
  buttonTitle='myButtonTitle' // required
  buttonVairant='secondary' // defaults to 'primary'
  modalTitle='myModalTitle' // required
  modalMessage='myWarningMessage' // required
  modalContinueButtonLabel='OK' // defaults to 'Continue'
  modalCancelButtonLabel='Go Back' // defaults to 'Cancel'
  onContinue={this.doSomething} // required
  />
 </React.Fragment>
 }
}
{code}

