Reported by [~alistairdoswald] :
Alistair Doswald: @Marek Posolda While writing my code, I've noticed a potential bug that will happen when someone will try to import a realm with users that have the "webauthn-register" required action. In the code to import a user RepresentationToModel.createUser(), there's the following code:
{code}
if (userRep.getRequiredActions() != null) {
  for (String requiredAction : userRep.getRequiredActions()) {
  user.addRequiredAction(UserModel.RequiredAction.valueOf(requiredAction.toUpperCase()));
  }
 }
{code}
Except that the WebAuthn required action is not in the UserModel.RequiredAction enum. We've encountered this problem with our own custom authenticators.
Alistair Doswald: I know someone on my team wanted to bring up this behaviour on the mailing list when we encountered the problem, but I don't remember if they got around to it

