description:
In Quarkus distribution we support keycloak.properties, system properties and environment variables as sources for config. It could be nice to be able to also pass command line parameters, and this could perhaps be done automatically supporting all properties in keycloak.properties this way.
Pattern would be command line parameter would be prefixed with 'kc.' and all '-' would be replaced with '.'.For example:
{code}
# bin/kc.sh --http-port=8080 
{code}
Would be the equivalent to:
{code}
# bin/kc.sh -Dkc.http.port=8080
{code}

full_text:
Automatic command line options for kc script in Quarkus

In Quarkus distribution we support keycloak.properties, system properties and environment variables as sources for config. It could be nice to be able to also pass command line parameters, and this could perhaps be done automatically supporting all properties in keycloak.properties this way.
Pattern would be command line parameter would be prefixed with 'kc.' and all '-' would be replaced with '.'.For example:
{code}
# bin/kc.sh --http-port=8080 
{code}
Would be the equivalent to:
{code}
# bin/kc.sh -Dkc.http.port=8080
{code}

description:
Quite a few configuration properties are named using camelCase notation, like e.g.:
{code:none}
theme.staticMaxAge=...
hostname.default.frontendUrl=...
connectionsJpa.XXX.dataSource=...
{code}
This is fine for configuration file and Java properties, but environment variable counterparts (provided OOTB by MP-Config) look ugly:
{code:none}
KEYCLOAK_THEME_STATICMAXAGE=...
KEYCLOAK_HOSTNAME_DEFAULT_FRONTENDURL=...
KEYCLOAK_CONNECTIONSJPA_XXX_DATASOURCE=...
{code}
For the properties like above, we should provide proper conversion of {{camelCase}} to {{UPPER_UNDERSCORE_CASE}}:
{code:none}
KEYCLOAK_THEME_STATIC_MAX_AGE=...
KEYCLOAK_HOSTNAME_DEFAULT_FRONTEND_URL=...
KEYCLOAK_CONNECTIONS_JPA_XXX_DATA_SOURCE=...
{code}
Additionally, we could also support alternate {{dash-case}} notation for config files, which seems to be more widely adopted than `camelCase` (by Spring Boot, Thorntail etc.):
{code:none}
theme.static-max-age=...
hostname.default.frontend-url=...
connections-jpa.XXX.data-source=...
{code}

full_text:
Improvements for camelCase config properties

Quite a few configuration properties are named using camelCase notation, like e.g.:
{code:none}
theme.staticMaxAge=...
hostname.default.frontendUrl=...
connectionsJpa.XXX.dataSource=...
{code}
This is fine for configuration file and Java properties, but environment variable counterparts (provided OOTB by MP-Config) look ugly:
{code:none}
KEYCLOAK_THEME_STATICMAXAGE=...
KEYCLOAK_HOSTNAME_DEFAULT_FRONTENDURL=...
KEYCLOAK_CONNECTIONSJPA_XXX_DATASOURCE=...
{code}
For the properties like above, we should provide proper conversion of {{camelCase}} to {{UPPER_UNDERSCORE_CASE}}:
{code:none}
KEYCLOAK_THEME_STATIC_MAX_AGE=...
KEYCLOAK_HOSTNAME_DEFAULT_FRONTEND_URL=...
KEYCLOAK_CONNECTIONS_JPA_XXX_DATA_SOURCE=...
{code}
Additionally, we could also support alternate {{dash-case}} notation for config files, which seems to be more widely adopted than `camelCase` (by Spring Boot, Thorntail etc.):
{code:none}
